1
00:00:06,450 --> 00:00:09,590
A projector shines a small picture onto a wall.

2
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:17,240
The picture on the wall is 3 times as wide as the original, and every line in it points back to the lamp.

3
00:00:17,290 --> 00:00:21,060
Is the picture on the wall the same shape as the original?

4
00:00:21,110 --> 00:00:24,240
Pause the video and choose.

5
00:00:24,290 --> 00:00:24,520
Yes.

6
00:00:24,570 --> 00:00:26,070
Only the size changes.

7
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:30,420
Every length is multiplied by 3, and the angles stay the same.

8
00:00:30,470 --> 00:00:33,080
This is called an enlargement.

9
00:00:33,130 --> 00:00:38,090
Remember: an enlargement with scale factor 2 doubles every length.

10
00:00:38,140 --> 00:00:44,110
A 4 centimetre side, enlarged by scale factor 3, becomes 12 centimetres.

11
00:00:44,160 --> 00:00:47,540
An enlargement changes the size, but not the shape.

12
00:00:47,590 --> 00:00:50,690
All lengths are multiplied by the scale factor.

13
00:00:50,740 --> 00:00:52,920
All angles stay the same.

14
00:00:52,970 --> 00:00:56,020
The centre of enlargement fixes the position.

15
00:00:56,070 --> 00:01:02,640
Each image vertex is the scale factor times as far from the centre as the object vertex.

16
00:01:02,690 --> 00:01:03,330
Your turn.

17
00:01:03,380 --> 00:01:06,500
In an enlargement, what happens to the angles?

18
00:01:06,550 --> 00:01:09,760
Pause the video and choose.

19
00:01:09,810 --> 00:01:11,360
The angles stay the same.

20
00:01:11,410 --> 00:01:15,590
The scale factor is the image length divided by the object length.

21
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:19,830
To find the centre, draw lines through pairs of matching vertices.

22
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:22,170
They all meet at the centre.

23
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:23,490
Here is the method.

24
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:28,690
Step 1: from the centre, count the steps across and up to a vertex.

25
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:32,750
Step 2: multiply those steps by the scale factor.

26
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:38,270
Step 3: count the new steps from the centre, and plot the image vertex.

27
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:42,880
Step 4: repeat for every vertex, then check the lengths.

28
00:01:42,930 --> 00:01:48,660
Enlarge the triangle 1, 1; 3, 1; 1, 2 by scale factor 3, centre 0, 0.

29
00:01:48,710 --> 00:01:56,000
With the origin as centre, just multiply every coordinate by 3: 3, 3; 9, 3; 3, 6.

30
00:01:56,050 --> 00:01:56,780
Your turn.

31
00:01:56,830 --> 00:02:00,200
Enlarge 4, 3 by scale factor 2, centre 2, 1.

32
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:03,310
Pause and work it out.

33
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:07,660
From the centre 2, 1 to 4, 3 is 2 across and 2 up.

34
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:10,440
Times 2 gives 4 across and 4 up.

35
00:02:10,490 --> 00:02:13,080
From 2, 1, that is 6, 5.

36
00:02:13,130 --> 00:02:18,780
A shape with a perimeter of 14 centimetres is enlarged by scale factor 4.

37
00:02:18,830 --> 00:02:26,270
Every length is multiplied by 4, so the perimeter is 14 times 4, which is 56 centimetres.

38
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:30,180
Ben enlarges 3, 2 by scale factor 2, centre 1, 1.

39
00:02:30,230 --> 00:02:32,970
Which line goes wrong first?

40
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:34,220
Line 2 is wrong.

41
00:02:34,270 --> 00:02:35,080
He added 2.

42
00:02:35,130 --> 00:02:39,700
You must multiply the steps by 2: 4 across and 2 up.

43
00:02:39,750 --> 00:02:42,440
From 1, 1, that is 5, 3.

44
00:02:42,490 --> 00:02:50,250
When a photo is enlarged from 10 by 15 centimetres to 20 by 30 centimetres, every length is doubled.

45
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:55,020
The scale factor is 2, so the picture keeps its shape.

46
00:02:55,070 --> 00:02:58,810
But a print of 20 by 25 would not be an enlargement.

47
00:02:58,860 --> 00:03:03,810
The shape would change, so part of the photo must be cut off.

48
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:05,090
One last question.

49
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:08,720
A side is 3 centimetres, and the scale factor is 5.

50
00:03:08,770 --> 00:03:10,650
How long is the image side?

51
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:13,970
Pause the video and answer.

52
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:17,280
3 times 5 is 15 centimetres.

53
00:03:17,330 --> 00:03:21,190
To remember: lengths are multiplied by the scale factor.

54
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:23,200
Angles do not change.

55
00:03:23,250 --> 00:03:28,090
Distances from the centre are multiplied by the scale factor too.

56
00:03:28,140 --> 00:03:33,120
The scale factor is the image length divided by the object length.

57
00:03:33,170 --> 00:03:37,240
Lines through matching vertices meet at the centre.

58
00:03:37,290 --> 00:03:42,670
Great work! Now practise lesson 14.6 on Camday.
